{"title":"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> be a real number. Consider the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10529df5c75836665db01d0d8bf3ae96ab0caf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(x_i^2+(a-x_i)^2)= na^2\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"47\" />\nHow many solutions (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2719960d803a38ff2560599c978b4acac5fbe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2 \\cdots , x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" />) does this equation have, such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b167df83780d55ba5dfb9c67b13a0fda5d96fd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\leq x_i \\leq a, i \\in N^+\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, rearrange the equation by expanding, simplifying, and using properties of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Summation\" title=\"Summation\">summation</a>.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe36d1024826abd0ac0bec2f24d392d8eb3913b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i^2 + a^2 - 2ax_i + x_i^2) &amp;= na^2 \\\\ \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (a^2 + 2x_i^2 - 2ax_i) &amp;= na^2 \\\\ na^2 + 2 \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i^2) - 2a \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i) &amp;= na^2 \\\\ 2 \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i^2) - 2a \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i) &amp;= 0 \\\\ \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i^2) - a \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_i) &amp;= 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"270\" height=\"279\" />\nNext, we can try smaller values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> to find patterns.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7746ed746b280e2a83d7defebe5cfe5d557fc9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />, then the equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e5a4515df8f16c140f19e02f53d5deff8420eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2 - ax_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3dc3ecf2fcb08b3ca53e2f8a39760158a8a63a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9dede0e9752caabb69f3be9dbe1852fe469c224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b763cbcce134c20ae9e2bfb823a1ef21a9eb8e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, we can graph the equation on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cartesian_plane\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cartesian plane\">Cartesian plane</a> (with axes as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />).  The equation is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, and from the bounds, the only solutions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f7649afc3d3a51caf97f60eed73ea07fe47d70b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0),(0,a),(a,0),(a,a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.  It seems as if the solution to the set involves only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  To prove this, we need to prove that solutions involving only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> would work and that no other solutions are possible.\n</p><p><br />\nFor the first part, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a>.  The base case is already covered since the solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/7746ed746b280e2a83d7defebe5cfe5d557fc9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3dc3ecf2fcb08b3ca53e2f8a39760158a8a63a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9dede0e9752caabb69f3be9dbe1852fe469c224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" />.  For the inductive step, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31b9656e752837a9046149cd658e183b9130cb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(x_i^2+(a-x_i)^2)= na^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"203\" height=\"53\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec020b09f33839d9c5190e7ead679afcc68d1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e531e3d2a6da0bcd0bc3940d5925f2e48ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" /> for integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b612c04916e1f37baeea775bdfcdab31a2fbe8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e4cbbb635d5bec59a75795e0c892d626429ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1}^2+(a-x_{i+1})^2 = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c349487a2a6a44e58b03a2a2152222d6827180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1} = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e4cbbb635d5bec59a75795e0c892d626429ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1}^2+(a-x_{i+1})^2 = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc03903f977e719c2a244468e3532f075546e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(x_i^2+(a-x_i)^2) + x_{i+1}^2+(a-x_{i+1})^2 = (n+1)a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"412\" height=\"53\" />.  The inductive step holds, so solutions are all ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bff80d36c501f381f93696cf58757931726649d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1, x_2, \\cdots x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec020b09f33839d9c5190e7ead679afcc68d1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e531e3d2a6da0bcd0bc3940d5925f2e48ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" /> for integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor the second part, note that we can complete the square for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e7249e3d174f9b9ee909eda3a3247435228dbecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1 - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 + (x_2 - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 + \\cdots (x_n - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 = \\tfrac{na^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"337\" height=\"24\" />.  We know that for integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d36f82b4d13fe00b2d1c7ee3a5c58430b0fa6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le x_i \\le a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92a20244f5ea887baf220582b90c91f427320df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\tfrac{a}{2} \\le x_i - \\tfrac{a}{2} \\le \\tfrac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196dfaa81042bdf68c9a7ae55cc5af6301468152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 \\le \\tfrac{a^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"111\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e531e3d2a6da0bcd0bc3940d5925f2e48ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec020b09f33839d9c5190e7ead679afcc68d1c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196dfaa81042bdf68c9a7ae55cc5af6301468152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 \\le \\tfrac{a^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"111\" height=\"24\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c908fc2e66f7cac3f0bb766ea8d5f05568ffb2b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i \\ne 0, a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf2e522b37cda95dc9ae065a3771633fb6860a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x_i &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84d85fdf89b8680ae3d27a5ae61685073d35f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 &lt; \\tfrac{a^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"111\" height=\"24\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e80454f8e2f9436f5571fec1afe7532f8bc105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x_1 &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252ca75f59513b92a73adb1cd26ad63660718885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1 - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 &lt; \\tfrac{a^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"113\" height=\"24\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a672fa3a49e9399b6ae48c574e769deaaa0119ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\tfrac{a}{2})^2 &lt; \\tfrac{na^2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"149\" height=\"53\" />, so there are no solutions where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c908fc2e66f7cac3f0bb766ea8d5f05568ffb2b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i \\ne 0, a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> in the solution to the original equation, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> can only equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e32bd4fa2a52f01181916df23f0c86cc7ec9785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" /> ordered pairs that are solutions to the equation.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO\">2001 Pan African MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pan_African_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Pan African MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Pan African MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163238\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 325/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 962/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10851/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.649      1 Template:Pan_African_MO_box\n100.00%   12.649      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17924:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163238 and revision id 113026. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}